WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:07.982
[Music starts] [Audio Description - not captioned]

00:00:08.892 --> 00:00:11.640
[Quynh Nguyen, PhD] This particular project,&nbsp;
funded by the National Library of Medicine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:18.660
is producing a new national data resource,&nbsp;
for built environment characteristics, using&nbsp;

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:25.543
Google Street View images and computer vision&nbsp;
models and to estimate the association between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.543 --> 00:00:29.273
built environment characteristics and&nbsp;
health outcomes on a national level.

00:00:38.762 --> 00:00:43.571
[Ming Hu] Built environment, in the simplest&nbsp;
way, is just everything human built.

00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:47.821
It includes the streets, all&nbsp;
the buildings, all the houses.

00:00:53.448 --> 00:00:57.883
[Thu Nguyen] We merged the Google Street&nbsp;
View image data with the patient&nbsp;data.

00:00:57.883 --> 00:01:01.440
So we looked at coronary artery&nbsp;
disease, hypertension, and diabetes.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.793
And then our model controlled for individual&nbsp;
characteristics such as like race, ethnicity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.793 --> 00:01:08.834
insurance status, English language ability.

00:01:12.209 --> 00:01:17.060
[Quynh Nguyen] In our pilot study, we merged&nbsp;
those indicators with patient data in Utah.&nbsp;

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.690
It was close to a million patient records.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.073
Healthcare systems want to know - what are&nbsp;
some exposures that their patients encounter?
 &nbsp;

00:01:27.073 --> 00:01:29.400
What are some of the predictors that can help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.395
them better understand where's the&nbsp;
chronic risk disease coming from?

00:01:36.598 --> 00:01:39.660
[Thu Nguyen] We found that like&nbsp;
greeners of streets, or visible wires,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:46.380
or dilapidated&nbsp;buildings predicted prevalence of&nbsp;
coronary artery disease and hypertension diabetes.

00:01:49.337 --> 00:01:54.300
[Quynh Nguyen] So crosswalk and sidewalks&nbsp;
are indicators of walkability. So the more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:58.320
walkable neighborhood is, the more&nbsp;
it encourages physical activity.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:03.523
We have other indicators like street&nbsp;
trees and street greenery which promote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:08.499
which we found are associated with,&nbsp;
lower obesity and better mental health.

00:02:08.686 --> 00:02:13.560
We made a geoportal where you can select the&nbsp;
neighborhood feature that you're interested in.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:21.900
You can also zoom into a location. So you&nbsp;
can type in address or a city and it'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.569
naturally zoom in and give you the distribution&nbsp;
of the characteristics at that neighborhood.

00:02:26.668 --> 00:02:31.020
People can interact with the data.&nbsp;
It allows for a quick analyses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.613
flexible boundaries, and publicly available.

00:02:33.709 --> 00:02:38.761
[Thu Nguyen] And it's a huge data source for for&nbsp;
the public health researchers and policy makers.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.639
[Ming Hu] Doing this way, it can give us &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.639 --> 00:02:48.405
first, a set of large data to show us what is the&nbsp;
impact of the building we design and we build.

00:02:48.493 --> 00:02:50.196
[Quynh Nguyen] Without NLM support,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.196 --> 00:02:54.000
we wouldn't have the protected&nbsp;
time that we had over five years.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.220
We wouldn't be able to purchase&nbsp;
the images and also purchase the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.700
the computing software and&nbsp;
hardware to run the models,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:08.368
and also the granted help support - doctoral&nbsp;
students - and fund their their entire studies.

00:03:10.897 --> 00:03:14.443
It takes a significant amount&nbsp;
of time to walk and inventory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.443 --> 00:03:17.206
neighborhood features of the built environment.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.440
And so that would not be possible if you&nbsp;
are interested in any place across the U.S.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.905
And thus, we need computer vision and Google&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.905 --> 00:03:28.560
Street View images to enable the&nbsp;
analyses at the national level.

00:03:28.982 --> 00:03:42.354
[Music]

00:03:43.976 --> 00:03:46.799
[Music fades to silence]

00:03:46.832 --> 00:03:47.552
[Silence]

